From 389ad4f455ece1f6a844ac8d6d40096a1abf9df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:22:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/32] feat(qsa): multi-group pending ring for verify windows
 > compress ratio

The pending index-key ring held exactly compress_ratio rows per request and was
addressed req_pool_idx * ratio + position % ratio. A forward that writes W
consecutive positions and compresses the group ending inside that window touches
up to W + ratio - 1 consecutive positions, so the ring aliases as soon as W > 1.

At the shipped W == ratio == 4 this is already wrong: a verify window covers every
residue class, so the group completing mid-window is compressed from the NEXT
groups tokens whenever the committed length is not a multiple of the ratio, i.e.
on three verify cycles out of four. It is silent, because the compressed key is
only consumed by the block-selection top-k.

Size the ring R = ratio * ceil((W + ratio - 1) / ratio) and address position % R,
in the eager builders, the CUDA-graph Triton kernel, the graph-replay host
fallback and the PD pending-state transfer infos (whose page is one requests
whole ring, not one group). Relax the target-verify guard to W <= R - ratio + 1.
W == 1 keeps the historical ratio-sized layout bit for bit.
SGLANG_QSA_PENDING_RING_SLOTS pins the old ring for an A/B against an older build.

topk > 1 is still rejected: tree verify multiplies the routed-expert union.

Adds 117 CPU tests that drive the production slot builders over prefill lengths,
verify widths 1-8, exhaustive accept patterns and rejection/rollback streams, and
that assert the ratio-sized ring aliases, so the sizing cannot be reverted quietly.
